## P1 — needed before running more than a handful of deals a month

139 items.

### 1.1 Money — Accounts, credentials and configuration (readiness gate)
- [ ] **(Eng)** `escrow_proof_links` WARN — set `PORTLESS_PUBLIC_BASE_URL` (public HTTPS address of the backend) and `ESCROW_PROOF_LINK_SECRET` so every stage release uploads a signed proof sheet to Tazapay.

### 1.2 Inspection, freight, customs — Accounts, credentials and configuration (readiness gate)
- [ ] **(Biz)** If SGS / Bureau Veritas will be offered: real booking-desk addresses in `SGS_BOOKING_EMAIL` / `BUREAU_VERITAS_BOOKING_EMAIL`, their webhook secrets, and `QC_PROVIDERS_ENABLED` updated (only QIMA is enabled today).
- [ ] **(Biz)** Freight forwarder for quotes and non-Maersk lanes: `COGOPORT_API_KEY` or `FREIGHTOS_API_KEY` (+ webhook secrets).

### 1.3 E-mail — Accounts, credentials and configuration (readiness gate)
- [ ] **(Ops)** `email_domain` WARN — send from your own domain (`PORTLESS_EMAIL_DOMAIN`) with SPF, DKIM and DMARC; a personal Gmail hurts deliverability and trust with buyers.
- [ ] **(Ops)** Separate mailboxes or aliases per role (trade desk, accounts, inspections) so replies route cleanly.

### 1.4 Documents and identity — Accounts, credentials and configuration (readiness gate)
- [ ] **(Ops)** `PORTLESS_MARINE_POLICY` (open marine policy number) for the insurance declaration on CIF deals.
- [ ] **(Ops)** Company profile for every e-mail: `PORTLESS_LEGAL_NAME`, `PORTLESS_SENDER_NAME` / `_TITLE`, `PORTLESS_WEBSITE`, `PORTLESS_PHONE`, `PORTLESS_CONTACT_EMAIL`.

### 1.5 Platform — Accounts, credentials and configuration (readiness gate)
- [ ] **(Ops)** `catalogue` WARN — load the real product lines and corridors (`PUT /trade-min/catalogue`); empty means the scanner runs built-in sample HS codes.
- [ ] **(Biz)** Telegram alerts: `HITL_TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN` / `HITL_TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID`, `DIGEST_EMAIL_TO`.
- [ ] **(Eng)** Make sure production never sets `INTEGRATION_MODE=sandbox`, `QC_SANDBOX_PROVIDERS`, `ESCROW_SANDBOX_PROVIDERS`, `CARRIER_SANDBOX_PROVIDERS` or `AUTO_FLOW_ENABLED` (readiness checks them; keep them in the deploy review).

### 2.1 Tazapay (escrow) — Provider contracts not yet confirmed
- [ ] **(Biz)** Confirm Tazapay's fee per transaction and per payout, settlement currency and timing, and the documents it accepts for each stage (proof sheet link vs files).

### 2.2 Escrow.com — Provider contracts not yet confirmed
- [ ] **(Eng)** Escrow.com signs no webhook — PortLess uses a URL token and re-reads the transaction. Confirm the milestone (one item per tranche) flow, buyer acceptance per milestone and the inspection period on a sandbox account.

### 2.3 Maersk (carrier) — Provider contracts not yet confirmed
- [ ] **(Eng)** Booking 2.0 fields beyond the minimum (`shipmentLocations`, `references`, `equipmentReferences`, `remarks`) and Track & Trace event-code field names follow DCSA — confirm Maersk accepts and returns them. Every endpoint path can be overridden in env.
- [ ] **(Ops/Eng)** Order of steps: in real shipping the carrier booking comes before container stuffing. Today freight is booked after QC and supervised loading (the compliance check needs the sealed container) and the stuffed container numbers are passed into the booking. Decide the real order with the trade desk: book space earlier (after PSI is scheduled), then attach containers and seals; if numbers differ from what Maersk holds, the VGM gate flags it.
- [ ] **(Eng)** Submit shipping instructions by API once Maersk confirms the endpoint, so the draft B/L does not need the portal.

### 2.4 QIMA (inspection) — Provider contracts not yet confirmed
- [ ] **(Eng)** QIMA has no webhook — results arrive by polling (`QC_POLL_MINUTES`). Confirm acceptable delay; consider a shorter poll on inspection day.
- [ ] **(Biz)** Confirm the product tree ids per HS code and the AQL / sample level for each commodity (QIMA defaults are for consumer goods, not grain).

### 2.5 Payoneer, ICEGATE, Stripe — Provider contracts not yet confirmed
- [ ] **(Eng)** ICEGATE — confirm the API access model (direct, via an aggregator, or via the CHA) and the Shipping Bill / LEO response format.

### 2.6 Data providers — Provider contracts not yet confirmed
