## Appendix — background per area

### 1 Accounts, credentials and configuration (readiness gate)

Each item is a failing or warning readiness check today.

### 2 Provider contracts not yet confirmed

Each provider was built from public documentation; these points were not confirmed by the provider and must be checked against a real account before money moves.

### 3 Legal, regulatory and trade compliance (India export)

PortLess is the exporter of record, buys from Indian suppliers and sells to foreign buyers. Every point needs a lawyer / chartered accountant's sign-off; the seed lists in the code are not the law.

### 5.5 Add suppliers manually (local suppliers)

The trade desk knows local suppliers that no scan will find. Today they cannot be added so that
the workflow takes over:
- the supplier directory (`trade_counterparties`) is written only by a scan — there is no add / edit endpoint and no console screen (buyers can be added to a deal, suppliers cannot);
- a deal created by hand with a supplier party but no scan opportunity gets **no RFQ**: the RFQ leg finds no candidates (`_rfq_candidates` reads only Match Engine results or the opportunity) and leaves the deal parked in MATCHING;
- `POST /deals/{id}/supplier-offers` (an offer entered by staff) runs neither the GST / IEC verification nor the match board — someone has to call `/match/evaluate` by hand.
Backend
Console (portless-ui)
QA

### 11 New features to raise profit per deal (product)

Ordered by expected impact on margin. Each should be measured on closed deals (realised margin vs cost sheet).
